    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today as several of our primary offensive anchors\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014are sidelined by a team-wide off-day, significantly thinning our available pool for the 5x5 categories. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining on the IL, our offensive output hinges on low-floor utility plays. **Andy Pages** (42.71) serves as our strongest individual start, though he faces a formidable challenge against Cease, whose 2.96 xERA dictates a tempered expectation. While **Andy Pages** maintains a steady base projection, his efficiency is hampered by an unfavorable batting order position (#8) and the high-skill profile of the opposition. **Drake Baldwin** (40.03) rounds out our active participants, operating at the absolute bottom of our starting threshold; despite solid recent xwOBA metrics, his utility is severely capped by the #9 lineup slot and a neutral platoon matchup against a top-tier arm.\n\nThe decision to bench our deeper roster reserves like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Lowe**, and **Jacob Wilson** was driven by the combination of poor park factors and lackluster matchup efficiency against tonight's starting pitching slate. **Heliot Ramos** was the closest to making the cut, but his raw projection failed to clear the 40-point hurdle due to a projected regression in contact quality against today's specific arm. We are prioritizing strict adherence to our efficiency floor to preserve game caps for higher-leverage matchups later in the week. Caution is advised as we navigate this lean roster day; should the official lineups shift **Drake Baldwin** or **Andy Pages** even lower in the order, we are prepared to pivot to a defensive substitution or a bench freeze to protect our cumulative batting average.",
